{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-frobenius-dual-h3","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:frobenius-dual-h3","kind":"definition","title":"Frobenius dual $K^\\vee$ in $H_3(q)$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-frobenius-gram-matrix"],"cites":["references/kassel1995"],"tags":["frobenius-dual","gram-matrix","hecke-algebra","markov-trace","non-degenerate"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.frobeniusDual","text":"frobenius-dual-h3.md","leanSource":"frobenius-dual-h3.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:frobenius-dual-h3\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G_{ij} = \\mathrm{tr}_M(b_i \\cdot b_j)</code> be the Gram matrix of the Frobenius pairing on the NF basis <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{b_i\\}</code> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_3(q)</code> (<a href=\"#prop:frobenius-gram-matrix\" data-at=\"mass-theory/mass-algebraic-consolidated/mass-algebraic-markov-gram\">Frobenius Gram matrix</a>), read at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z = q^3/(q^2+1)</code> on the quotient <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_3/\\mathrm{rad}\\,\\mathrm{tr}_M \\cong \\mathrm{TL}_3</code>, where the induced pairing is non-degenerate. For a state <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K = \\sum_i c_i b_i</code> in NF, the <strong>Frobenius dual</strong> is the unique element <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K^\\vee \\in H_3(q)</code> satisfying <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\langle K^\\vee, b_j \\rangle_F = c_j</code> for all <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">j</code>. Explicitly:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  K^\\vee = \\sum_{i,j} c_i (G^{-1})_{ij} b_j.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-dual-h3.md","heading":"Definition","number":"13.4.21","page":"b/def-frobenius-dual-h3","qa":{"counts":{"pass":84,"fail":3,"warn":2,"na":16,"unknown":0,"stale":77},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassTheory.Archimedean.frobeniusDual","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-dual-h3.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
